From 6a2ec08c9a9e08b8347913f0b0f31ce5fc5e9c9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:24:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): hub claim screen defers edited and over-budget
 cards [daveey]

Follow-ups from the review of #1637 (t_01a1d2182f7e6a73 at c8784b80c6):

1. A card edited while the judge ran had its verdict skipped by _apply, yet
   stayed ready and label-less, so the same tick's claim pass claimed it
   unjudged on the hub. screen() now records it in Counts.deferred_ids; the
   dispatcher leaves those ids out of this tick's ready lane, and the next
   tick judges the new snapshot.
2. screen() judged every eligible card serially (30 s timeout each; ~27
   backlog cards at rollout). It now makes at most MAX_JUDGED_PER_TICK (3)
   judge calls per tick; the rest are deferred the same way, never claimed
   unjudged. A judge outage still fails open once per tick as before.

worker_pickup/safe_screen return the deferred ids (empty off the hub, on dry
runs and when the screen fails). Tests: edit-during-judge regression (not
claimed this tick, judged and claimed next tick, no unjudged claim) and a
N > cap backlog test (cap judge calls, no unjudged claims, rest judged next
tick); both are RED without the dispatcher filter.
